{%- comment -%}
  Bush Riding product hero. Full-bleed product-in-action photograph, then the
  two-up under it — the same full-bleed language as the home hero, doing the
  visual work so the buy controls can live in the rail (desktop) or below the
  fold (phone) without the photography ever sharing a screen with them.

  It used to draw its own wordmark + Explore bar across the top of the
  photograph, and later its own <h1> caption. Both duplicated something the
  page already had. This band is a photograph, nothing else.

  Sits above `main` in templates/product.json; only makes sense on the
  product template, so it always reads from the `product` object.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section class="alp alp-phero">
  <div class="alp-phero__media">
    {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
      {{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 2400 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high', alt: section.settings.image.alt | default: '' }}
    {%- elsif product.featured_image != blank -%}
      {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 2400 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high', alt: '' }}
    {%- else -%}
      <img src="{{ 'alpine-ph-hero.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="800" height="1000" loading="eager"
        data-asset-note="Full-bleed product-in-action photograph — the rider wearing/using this product on the trail">
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The caption that used to sit here carried its own <h1>, which meant the page
    had two — this one and main-product's title block. Turns 8b and 9d put the
    title in the rail on desktop and in the copy block on a phone, so the
    photograph is now just a photograph and there is exactly one h1.
  {%- endcomment -%}
</section>

{%- comment -%}
  Name and price, directly under the lead image — PHONES ONLY.

  On desktop the rail carries these and the field stays photography. There is
  no rail on a phone, so without this you landed on a product, scrolled past a
  lead image and a two-up, and still did not know what the thing was called or
  what it cost: the only price on the first screen was inside the buy bar.
  Turn 9d puts them here for exactly that reason.

  This is the h1 at phone widths and Dawn's own title block is hidden there
  (alpine.css), so precisely one heading is ever exposed.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product != blank -%}
  <div class="alp alp-phero__id">
    <h1 class="alp-phero__name">{{ product.title | escape }}</h1>
    <p class="alp-phero__price">
      {%- if product.price_varies -%}From {% endif -%}
      {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | money }}
    </p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The two-up under the lead image, split by a 3px mist gap — the same rule that
  divides every other section. Only drawn when the product actually has more
  photographs; one image is a lead, not a gallery.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign extra = product.images | slice: 1, 2 -%}
{%- if extra.size > 1 -%}
  <div class="alp alp-phero__pair">
    {%- for image in extra -%}
      {{ image | image_url: width: 1200 | image_tag: class: 'alp-phero__pairshot', loading: 'lazy', alt: image.alt | default: '' }}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Bush Riding product hero",
  "tag": "div",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Full-bleed band above the buy block. Falls back to the product's featured image, then a placeholder, if no image is set here." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image", "info": "Leave blank to use the product's featured image." }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Bush Riding product hero" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
